<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49260" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trŏchĭlus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόχιλος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A very small bird</i>, perh. <i>the
				golden-crested wren</i>, <i>trochil</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 10,
				74, 95, § 203</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 25, 37, §
			90</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In architecture, <i>a semicircular hollow running round
				the base of a column</i>, <i>a casement</i>, <i>scotia</i>, <i>trochil</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 3, 3 <i>med.</i></span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
